This is a collection of YANIs by users of the #nethack IRC channel on
freenode.net. Please excuse any old ideas that may be present.

[1]: Scrolls of identify should be a lot more expensive. Knowledge is
power. --Grunt

[2]: This is a bug: When wielded a shield of reflection doesn't reflect
--scwizard

[3]: When #dipping or diluting a smoky potion by any other means, there
should be the chance of a djinni appearing, most likely hostle. I mean,
who here enjoys having cold water dumped on them when they're trying to
sleep? --LordMatthius

[4]: A scroll of charging on the ground should untame any q, or u - it
makes them charge. --SpeedEvil

[5]: new scroll : polymorph. high base price range(350-400). when
uncursed and on self acts like a polytrap, when given direction acts
like /oPoly. When blessed, on self acts like you have poly control,
same as uncursed otherwise. Cursed acts like polytrap but does not ask
direction, targets self automatically. Confused : cursed targets random
object(s) in inventory and polys them --Xarann

[6]: Continued..., uncursed acts like you zap /oPoly in random
direction around you, blessed targets {some_armor}, makes it
"polyproof/shapefitting"(armor that doesn't break when you poly into
something too big) --Xarann

[7]: If you eat with a very high nutrition (say >1800) - instead of
choking, you explode. --SpeedEvil

[8]: Have everything on the map change colours when hallucinating.
(Everything really does look cosmic! And it looks boring afterwards,
too.) --Grunt

[9]: Some ill status effects could time out gradually, i.e. has only a
chance of impacting an action related to the numbers of turns it has to
time out. (For the hallucination idea just listed the map could
gradually return to normal.) --Grunt

[10]: A used up amulet of life saving should also act as a restore
ability. I mean, c'mon: If you lose your head, it gives you your whole
head back. If you lose your brains, you only get 3 points back.
--TheShrewdDude

[11]: You should be able to wish for Chromatic Dragon scales. It gives
you resistance to... nothing, but it looks cool! (When placed on the
ground, it changes colours. Yeah.) --TheShrewdDude

[12]: Ring of Disintegration: Every n500 turns, you begin the
disintegration process, much like stoning or sliming. This can only be
cured by gremlin attack, praying, putting on a bdsm, gaining
disintegration resistance, or putting on a ring of gain constitution.
--TheShrewdDude

[13]: There is a portal to ancient Yendor in there somewhere. If you go
there, try to destroy the Amuletsmith, or sacrifice him to your god.
--TheShrewdDude

[14]: Using wands should require you to wield them. Or at least give a
bonus for wielding wands. --TheShrewdDude

[15]: As should markers. --SpeedEvil

